====Hell Rotor====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=kevin_214A,kevin_214C,kevin_214AC,kevin_214P_K
|input=214A/C/AC
|input2=qcb+A/C/AC
|description4= Charge up (or abort) a fierce backfist strike, then launch the attack by releasing the attack button or after a maximum charge time is reached.
* Press any kick button during the charge to cancel without attacking (minimum total animation length is 17 frames, or 16 for REV version). This is referred to as a Rotor Cancel.
* All versions and charge levels cause a knockdown on normal hit / Wild Punish and cause a slow launch on counterhit, with only one exception (see 214A below)
* A Rotor Cancel can be used as a Guard Cancel to force any attack to inflict only 17 frames of blockstun, opening up dangerous new punish opportunities. [https://dreamcancel.com/wiki/Fatal_Fury:_City_of_the_Wolves/Kevin_Rian/Strategy#Defense Read more about it here.]
----
'''Light version (214A):''' Swing a long backfist strike with huge horizontal range. Used as a long-range poke, but can also be used as a light confirm and/or combo ender. 
* All special-cancelable attacks can combo into this on a normal hit except for Far A, which can still combo into it if Far A hits as a counterhit / Wild Punish
* Good spacing makes this very difficult or downright impossible to punish despite being -6 on block for the uncharged version.
* As an exception to the above note on 214P granting knockdowns, an uncharged hit will leave the opponent grounded, even on counterhit / Wild Punish (where it becomes +9 instead of +4). An uncharged counterhit against an airborne enemy causes slow launch, and an uncharged airborne wild punish causes a knockdown.
----
'''Heavy version (214C):''' Bring down a slow, heavy overhead fist. Used as a close-range mixup tool.
* Only combos from Close C/D, but also frametraps from these normals on block
* Knocks the opponent straight down instead of away from Kevin
* If fully charged, Kevin steps forward far enough to make this hit from a bit further than round start distance, in addition to becoming safe on block
----
'''REV version (214AC):''' A 2-hit strike with an animation that looks a bit like a faster 214C followed by a shorter 214A. Used in combos, but can also be used to end blockstrings if braked.
* Despite the animation, the first hit is not an overhead
* Can be braked on the first hit to remain plus on block. Otherwise, punishable if not braked or REV Accel canceled into another REV special.
* A Rotor Cancel from this version is 1 frame faster than the normal versions of 214P

}}

====Hell Snipe====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=kevin_236A,kevin_236C,kevin_236AC
|input=236A/C/AC
|input2=qcf+A/C/AC
|description3= Kevin leaps into the air and swings his fist down on the opponent.

'''All versions:'''
* Can jump over attacks and potentially score a Wild Punish, starting a combo
* Very tall hitbox, capable of hitting full jumping and crouching opponents reliably
* Regardless of hit or block, gains an additional 3 frames of advantage against a crouching opponent
* Combos into 2A or Far A on grounded counterhit / Wild Punish, or Close C if the opponent is crouching. Causes big launch if it counterhits an airborne opponent
----
'''Light version (236A):''' Used to safely end blockstrings while inflicting good damage to the opponent's REV meter.
* About the same jump angle as a forward hop
* Will never jump over an opponent, even if they are knocked down
----
'''Heavy version (236C):''' Used to quickly approach an opponent or contest air space.
* About the same jump height as a forward jump, but travels a bit further
* Can jump over a crouching opponent and whiff if they are too close
* Can also be used as a combo ender following a braked 214AC hit
----
'''REV version (236AC):''' Used to remain plus on block and inflict heavy damage to the opponent's REV meter.
* Identical animation and jump angle to the light version, but deals more damage and is always plus on block
* Strangely, more advantageous on block than on hit (+2 vs +1)

}}

