'''1-bar version (236236B):''' 
* Launches the opponent, allowing a combo to continue (or start) with an additional 25% of combo scaling applied
* Does not have any invulnerability and cannot be used as a reversal unless it is used as a [https://dreamcancel.com/wiki/Fatal_Fury:_City_of_the_Wolves/Defense#Guard_Cancel Zero Frame Super], but is exceptionally rewarding in this case as it still functions as a combo-starting reversal
* Any ground normal can be canceled into '''236236K''' to start a combo except for 2D. 6B and 5CR cannot directly cancel into '''236236K''', but a counterhit / Wild Punish on either of these attacks allows them to combo into other normals, which can then be super-canceled.
* Not the most reliable anti-air despite the attack angle, especially when 2CR can combo into 236236K anyway
----
'''2-bar version (236236D):'''
* Unlike 236236B, this super is fully invulnerable and can be used as a reversal
* On grounded hit, opponent remains in a lengthy hitstun animation on the ground, giving Kevin enough time to move in and hit Close D to continue the combo. On airborne hit, launches even higher and slower than a counterhit launch
* Still not great at covering the air space above Kevin
}}

